{
  "name": "How to Plan Your Perfect Walk-In Shower Installation",
  "step": [
    {
      "name": "Step 1",
      "text": "Thinking about a walk-in shower? That’s great! They really open up a bathroom and can add a lot of style and functionality. But before you jump in, a little planning goes a long way to making sure you love the end result. First off, really think about your bathroom's layout. Will a walk-in shower fit nicely, or will it feel cramped? We’ve seen all kinds of spaces, and there’s usually a great solution, even for smaller bathrooms. Next, consider the drainage. This isn’t just about the look; it's super important for preventing leaks. You want to make sure the drain location and slope are spot-on. Then, get into the fun stuff: finishes and materials! Do you want tile, a solid surface, or something else? Each choice has its own considerations for installation and long-term care. Finally, remember that while some parts might seem DIY-friendly, anything involving plumbing, waterproofing, or structural changes really benefits from a pro's touch. Improper installation can lead to costly headaches like leaks and mold down the line. If you’re in the Denver area, give us a call at 303-505-0866 for a chat about your vision and how we can help bring it to life.",
      "@type": "HowToStep",
      "position": 1
    }
  ],
